只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Synchronize and Orchestrate agents from CLI to GUI, across desktop to phone.","id":"gh:1327124384","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"cosyncing","slug":"cosyncing/cosyncing","topics":["ade","agent-orchestration","agents","ai-agents","ai-agents-framework","ai-agents-platform","claude-code","codex","codex-cli","dsh-plugin","ide","opencode","orchestration","pi"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Synchronize and Orchestrate agents from CLI to GUI, across desktop to phone."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"From CLI to GUI, live and in sync"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Website ·\nInstall ·\nClient ·\nDocs ·\nContributing ·\n简体中文 ·\n日本語 ·\n한국어 ·\nEspañol"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Synchronize and control your agents — from CLI to GUI, from desktop to phone. Pick up right where yo"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"u left\noff, anywhere. cosyncing keeps your coding agents in sync across your own network."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"The broker runs on the machine where your agents work. It watches their sessions and serves\na client"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" that shows each one — grouped by project, with its transcript, diffs, commands, and any\nprompt wait"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ing on you. Read a session, answer a prompt, or take over. No account to create, no\nhosted service b"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"etween the client and the broker."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Supported agents"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"One protocol covers all twelve. Per-agent control differs: a Claude Code session in your own termina"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"l\nsyncs with the app in both directions, including approvals, once setup installs its mod; without t"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"he mod it opens read-only until\nyou take over. See supported-agent setup for versions and\ninstallati"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"on, and adapter support for the capability matrix."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Foreground clients can join the same broker-owned Codex, Pi, omp, or Reasonix Drive session without "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"starting a\nsecond native Resume. A Claude Code session without the mod keeps its Observe/Take-over f"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"low on\nanother client, while OpenCode keeps its shared-live behavior. Background Observe connections"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"lient, while OpenCode keeps its shared-live behavior. Background Observe connections stay read-only."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Experimental:** Eight provisional adapters are available to source contributors.\nKimi Code observe"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"s every session on a\n`kimi web` server read-only, drives the ones cosyncing created — prompts, appro"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"vals, model selection —\nand takes over the ones it did not, explicitly. DeepSeek Harness\nconnects to"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" a `dsh web` host and gives active foreground clients a shared transcript and control\nsurface, with "},{"id":"p9s5","text":"model and reasoning-effort selection, permission presets, the host's own slash commands,\nand image a"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"ttachments. General file attachments are not supported — the host accepts image content\nonly — and b"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ackground resident subscriptions and some message presentation remain follow-up work.\nAntigravity re"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"ads the Antigravity CLI's own conversation\nstore — no server involved — replays every conversation r"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"ead-only, and drives one through a\nbroker-owned `agy` child; two clients can share a Drive, and a wr"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ite from a terminal hands the\nsession back. omp uses its own packaged bridge and native RPC\ndialect "},{"id":"p9s11","text":"for discovery, live sync, prompts, approvals, commands, models, file input, and session\ncreation. Re"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"asonix observes its bounded local store and resumes\nthrough a lazy broker-owned ACP child; joined cl"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"ients share one writer, while terminal true sync and\nfile input remain unsupported. Grok Build obser"},{"id":"p9s14","text":"ves its bounded\nlocal store and, on 1.0.13 or newer, adds authenticated broker-owned ACP Create/Resu"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"me, prompts,\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Prerequisites"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The server runs with Bun 1.4.3 or newer. The one-command installers acquire it\nwhen needed; Node.js/"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"npm are not required. The broker is local-only by\ndefault. Cross-device use requires a proxy, tunnel"},{"id":"p11s3","text":", VPN,\nmesh network, or another operator-owned connectivity method.\nFor a simple private route, see "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"Tailscale Serve; for a\nself-managed overlay, see WireGuard or EasyTier. After\n`cosyncing setup`, you"},{"id":"p11s5","text":" can also copy\n`https://github.com/cosyncing/cosyncing/tree/main/docs/connectivity` to a coding agen"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"t and ask it to\nconfigure your chosen method while keeping the broker bound to loopback.\nTokdash is "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"optional but strongly recommended for quota\ntracking and warnings."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"See installation prerequisites for Linux and macOS commands,\nWSL notes, and Tokdash setup. For the s"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"igned one-liner installers, see\ninstalling with cosyncing's own installer."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The package contains one JavaScript application bundle and the web client. Supported broker hosts\nar"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"e Linux x64, Linux arm64, Apple Silicon macOS, and Windows x64. Windows ARM64 is not qualified\nyet, "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"and the broker refuses it — including an x64 process running under ARM64 emulation."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Before setup, install only the agents you use; see [agent setup and PATH\npreflight](docs/supported_a"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"gents/README.md#preflight)."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Install the current release with one command:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Linux / Apple Silicon macOS:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Windows x64 (PowerShell):"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Windows 11 x64 is supported. Windows 10 is not supported: Microsoft Defender may classify the\ninstal"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ler as a Trojan, and you should not disable Defender to force installation."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The installer verifies the release, installs the broker and a supported desktop client, then\nruns in"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"teractive setup and pairs the client. Headless Linux and Linux arm64 receive the server\nwithout a de"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"sktop client. Bun is acquired when needed; Node.js/npm are not required. See the\ninstaller guide for"},{"id":"p22s4","text":" broker-only commands, unattended\ninstallation and signed-channel updates."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"npm distribution ended at **0.6.6**; use the installers above for new installations or migration."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### After setup"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"`cosy pair --broker-url https://cosy.example.com` includes that client-reachable origin in a\nfive-mi"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"nute, one-use QR code. The URL is not persisted or probed. Omit the flag for an\nauthentication-only "},{"id":"p25s3","text":"offer when the client already knows its broker URL. See the\nconnectivity chooser. Scan the QR from a"},{"id":"p25s4","text":" client to grant access;\n`cosy devices list` lists paired devices, and `cosy devices revoke <id>` re"},{"id":"p25s5","text":" grant access;\n`cosy devices list` lists paired devices, and `cosy devices revoke <id>` revokes one."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"After setup, `cosy doctor` diagnoses the machine without changing it, and `cosy status` summarizes\ni"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"nstall, service, agents, and sessions."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Privacy and security"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The broker runs on your machine, under your account. Broker state is stored there; session content\ni"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"s sent only to authenticated clients over the network you choose. cosyncing operates no hosted\nservi"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ce in that connection path and includes no analytics or advertising telemetry. Optional\nfeatures con"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"tact only the services they name, such as local Tokdash quota data. cosyncing does not\nconfigure or "},{"id":"p28s5","text":"contact connectivity providers; any proxy, tunnel, VPN, or mesh is operator-owned.\nRun `cosy update`"},{"id":"p28s6","text":" to update an installer-owned broker and its recorded desktop client."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Report vulnerabilities through GitHub private vulnerability reporting, per SECURITY.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
